  "text": "Trish E. Paulos, DVM, MS, DACVIM (Oncology) - MedVet Salt Lake City\nFor Pet Parents\nFor Veterinarians\nWork at MedVet\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nSpecialties\nResources\nAbout\nFind a Clinic\nSpecialties\nVet Resources\nAbout\nMedVet Training Programs\nFind a Clinic\nReferral Partner Login\nRefer a Patient\nLocations\nFind A Doctor\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSocial Work\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSocial Work\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nReferral Partner Resources\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFor Pet Parents\nFind Care\nSpecialties\nResources\nAbout\nFor Veterinarians\nSpecialties\nVet Resources\nAbout\nMedVet Training Programs\nWork at MedVet\nEmergency Care\nRefer a Patient\nFind a Doctor\nTrish E. Paulos\nTrish E. Paulos, DVM, MS, DACVIM (Oncology)\nBoard-Certified Veterinary Oncologist\nTrish E. Paulos, DVM, MS, Diplomate, ACVIM (Oncology), is a Board-Certified\nVeterinary Oncologist\nat\nMedVet Salt Lake City\n, where she has been part of the team since 2025.\nDr. Paulos earned a Bachelor of Fine Arts degree in photography from the University of Utah. She then earned her Doctor of Veterinary Medicine degree from Washington State University College of Veterinary Medicine and a Master of Clinical Science degree from Colorado State University. Following veterinary school, she completed an internship in rotating medicine and surgery at Artemis Veterinary Emergency and Specialty Services, an internship in surgery at Sierra Veterinary Specialists, an internship in medical oncology at The Animal Medical Center in New York City, and an internship in combined medical and surgical oncology at VCA Canada Mississauga-Oakville. Dr. Paulos then completed a residency in Medical Oncology at Colorado State University.\nHer special interests include hospice and palliative care, oncology, pain management, quality of life support, and the human-animal bond. Dr. Paulos is passionate about helping families gain more time with their beloved pets while ensuring each patient lives with dignity and comfort throughout their care. In addition to her clinical work, she has authored publications on soft tissue sarcoma and metastatic nasal adenocarcinoma.\nWhen not treating patients, Dr. Trish Paulos enjoys aerial dance, rock climbing, and roller derby.\nEducation & Training\nBachelor of Fine Arts:\nUniversity of Utah\nDoctor of Veterinary Medicine:\nWashington State University College of Veterinary Medicine\nMaster of Clinical Science:\nColorado State University\nInternship (Rotating Medicine and Surgery):\nArtemis Veterinary Emergency and Specialty Services\nInternship (Surgery):\nSierra Veterinary Specialists\nInternship (Medical Oncology):\nThe Animal Medical Center\nInternship (Combined Medical and Surgical Oncology):\nVCA Canada Mississauga-Oakville\nResidency (Medical Oncology):\nColorado State University\nSpecializations\nDiplomate, American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (Oncology)\nAssociations\nAmerican College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (ACVIM)\nAmerican Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA)\nInternational Association for Animal Hospice and Palliative Care (IAAHPC)\nVeterinary Cancer Society (VCS)\nVeterinary Society of Surgical Oncology (VSSO)\nSpecialties\nMedical Oncology\nServicing Locations\nMedVet Salt Lake City\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
